     "ready": true,
     "rules": "Tesseract. Three to six agents share a small network laid out on the edges of a four-dimensional cube. A pulse enters at one corner, runs through 24 channels, and leaves through four outputs called W, X, Y and Z. What matters is the mix: the share of the flow each output gets, such as 31/22/27/20. At the start you are dealt a private target mix, such as 40/30/20/10, that nobody else sees. There are five rounds. Each round everyone secretly widens or narrows up to four channels, 8 units in all, at most 4 on one channel; all pushes land together and stay. Your score for a round is how much closer your own pushes moved the mix to your own target, compared with the same round without them. Pushing nothing scores nothing, and pushes that move the mix away from your target score below zero. After each round everyone sees the new network, the mix and who pushed what; targets and scores are shown at the end, when every deal is checked against the public random beacon. Highest total wins.",
